From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:03:27 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: gtactive3wifi: make install-to-userdata.sh safe and
 actually verify

- The verify step could never pass: the bring-up console's "cat" streams the
  whole block device (initramfs/init.c "cat " handler: read until EOF), so
  tab-get read the image length and then waited for the "> " trailer while
  buffering the rest of the 52 GiB partition in host RAM. Read exactly the
  image length and close the connection instead (the serving child dies on
  EPIPE/SIGPIPE, init forks one per connection).
- The verify trap ran rm -f "${RAW##*/}": a file in the current directory
  with the image's basename, i.e. the user's own image when installing an
  uncompressed .raw from its directory. Drop the traps; decompress next to
  the image instead of into /tmp (tmpfs, too small for ~6.4 GiB).
- tab-put read the whole image into memory and its "ok N"/"error" reply
  was never checked. Stream in 1 MiB chunks and require "ok <len>".
- Check on the device that sda31 is PARTNAME=userdata and a partition
  before writing (read on this unit: PARTN=31, PARTNAME=userdata), refuse
  images without a 4K-sector GPT, and require drop_caches to succeed so the
  read-back comes from UFS.
- Take build/tab.lock for every console access.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../install-to-userdata.sh                    | 164 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 126 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/install-to-userdata.sh b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/install-to-userdata.sh
index 98181b2..8a55d7a 100644
--- a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/install-to-userdata.sh
+++ b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/install-to-userdata.sh
@@ -3,15 +3,22 @@
 # the Galaxy Tab Active3, over the bring-up debug console, and verify it.
 #
 # The device must be sitting in the gtactive3-mainline bring-up console
-# (S-Boot -> uniLoader -> mainline Linux + nolibc init), which exposes the
-# "put PATH LEN" (host -> device raw stream) and "cat PATH" (device -> host
-# raw stream) commands over USB. This script uses the repo's tab/tab-put/
-# tab-get helpers, so the USB network must be up ("tab wait").
+# (S-Boot -> uniLoader -> mainline Linux + nolibc init, initramfs/init.c),
+# which serves TCP 23 on fe80::57:aff:fe00:1 over the USB NCM link with:
+#   "put PATH LEN" + LEN raw bytes  -> opens PATH O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC and
+#                                       writes them, replies "ok <received>"
+#   "cat PATH"                       -> streams PATH until EOF, then "> "
+# "cat" of a block device streams the WHOLE device (52 GiB for sda31), so the
+# read-back below reads exactly the image length and then closes the
+# connection; the console child that served it dies on SIGPIPE, init keeps
+# serving new connections (one fork per connection).
 #
 # Duranium lives in a GPT nested at the very start of sda31; the image is the
-# first ~6-7 GiB of that disk (ESP + usr + verity). First boot grows the
-# partitions into the full 52 GiB via systemd-repart, so only the image size
-# is written here, not the whole partition.
+# first ~6.4 GiB of that disk (ESP + usr + verity). First boot grows the
+# partitions into the full partition via systemd-repart, so only the image is
+# written, not the whole partition.
+#
+# Every console access takes build/tab.lock, like scripts/tab users must.
 #
 # Usage:
 #   install-to-userdata.sh IMAGE            # IMAGE is .raw or .raw.zst / .zst
@@ -20,22 +27,35 @@ set -euo pipefail
 
 ROOT=${GTA3_ROOT:-/home/borysthebear/Projects/gtactive3-mainline}
 TAB=$ROOT/scripts/tab
-TAB_PUT=$ROOT/scripts/tab-put
-TAB_GET=$ROOT/scripts/tab-get
-DEV=/dev/sda31          # Android userdata, confirmed in HARDWARE.md
+LOCK=$ROOT/build/tab.lock
+LL=fe80::57:aff:fe00:1
+PART=sda31              # Android userdata (HARDWARE.md "Partitions")
+DEV=/dev/$PART
+WANT_PARTNAME=userdata  # GPT name read on the device: sda31 uevent PARTNAME
 IMG=${1:?usage: install-to-userdata.sh IMAGE [--no-verify]}
 VERIFY=1
 [ "${2:-}" = "--no-verify" ] && VERIFY=0
 
-command -v zstd >/dev/null || { echo "zstd required" >&2; exit 1; }
+tab() { flock "$LOCK" "$TAB" "$@"; }
+
+ncm_iface() {
+	for d in /sys/class/net/*; do
+		[ "$(basename "$(readlink -f "$d/device/driver" 2>/dev/null)")" = cdc_ncm ] &&
+			{ basename "$d"; return 0; }
+	done
+	return 1
+}
 
-# Decompress to a plain raw image if needed.
+# Decompress next to the image (not into /tmp, which is a RAM-backed tmpfs on
+# the host and too small for ~6.4 GiB).
 case "$IMG" in
 	*.zst)
-		RAW=$(mktemp --suffix=.raw)
-		trap 'rm -f "$RAW"' EXIT
-		echo "Decompressing $IMG -> $RAW"
-		zstd -d -f -o "$RAW" "$IMG"
+		RAW=${IMG%.zst}
+		[ "$RAW" != "$IMG" ] || RAW=$IMG.raw
+		if [ ! -f "$RAW" ] || [ "$IMG" -nt "$RAW" ]; then
+			echo "Decompressing $IMG -> $RAW"
+			zstd -d -f -o "$RAW" "$IMG"
+		fi
 		;;
 	*)
 		RAW=$IMG
@@ -43,35 +63,106 @@ case "$IMG" in
 esac
 
 LEN=$(stat -c %s "$RAW")
+[ $((LEN % 4096)) -eq 0 ] || { echo "ERROR: image size $LEN is not a multiple of 4096 (UFS sector)" >&2; exit 1; }
 echo "Image: $RAW ($LEN bytes)"
+WANT=$(sha256sum "$RAW" | cut -d' ' -f1)
+echo "sha256 $WANT"
+
+# The nested GPT must use the UFS logical sector size (4096), else neither
+# U-Boot's blkmap nor the Linux loop device can parse it.
+python3 -I - "$RAW" <<'PY'
+import sys
+with open(sys.argv[1], "rb") as f:
+    hdr = f.read(8192)
+if hdr[4096:4104] != b"EFI PART":
+    sys.exit("ERROR: no GPT header at byte 4096: image is not a 4K-sector GPT disk")
+print("GPT: 4096-byte sectors")
+PY
 
 echo "Waiting for the tablet's USB console..."
-"$TAB" wait
+tab wait
 
-# Sanity: confirm the target exists and show its size (in 512-byte sectors).
-SECT=$("$TAB" "cat /sys/class/block/sda31/size" | tr -dc 0-9)
+# Sanity: the target must be the userdata partition and large enough.
+UEVENT=$(tab "cat /sys/class/block/$PART/uevent")
+echo "$UEVENT" | grep -qx "PARTNAME=$WANT_PARTNAME" || {
+	echo "ERROR: $DEV is not PARTNAME=$WANT_PARTNAME:" >&2; echo "$UEVENT" >&2; exit 1; }
+echo "$UEVENT" | grep -qx "DEVTYPE=partition" || { echo "ERROR: $DEV is not a partition" >&2; exit 1; }
+SECT=$(tab "cat /sys/class/block/$PART/size" | tr -dc 0-9)
 PARTBYTES=$(( SECT * 512 ))
-echo "Target $DEV: $PARTBYTES bytes ($SECT sectors)"
+echo "Target $DEV (PARTNAME=$WANT_PARTNAME): $PARTBYTES bytes"
 if [ "$LEN" -gt "$PARTBYTES" ]; then
 	echo "ERROR: image ($LEN) is larger than $DEV ($PARTBYTES)" >&2
 	exit 1
 fi
 
+IFC=$(ncm_iface) || { echo "tablet USB network not present" >&2; exit 1; }
+
 echo "Streaming image into $DEV ..."
-# tab-put opens the path for writing and streams exactly LEN bytes into it.
-# For a block device the create/truncate flags are no-ops; the bytes land at
-# offset 0, which is where the nested GPT begins.
-"$TAB_PUT" "$RAW" "$DEV"
-"$TAB" "write /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches 3" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
+flock "$LOCK" python3 -I - "$LL%$IFC" "$RAW" "$DEV" "$LEN" <<'PY'
+import socket, sys, time
+addr, local, remote, n = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3], int(sys.argv[4])
+s = socket.create_connection((addr, 23), timeout=30)
+buf = b""
+while not buf.endswith(b"> "):
+    d = s.recv(4096)
+    if not d:
+        sys.exit("console closed before the prompt")
+    buf += d
+s.sendall(f"put {remote} {n}\n".encode())
+t0 = time.time()
+sent = 0
+with open(local, "rb") as f:
+    while sent < n:
+        chunk = f.read(min(1 << 20, n - sent))
+        if not chunk:
+            sys.exit(f"short read of {local} at {sent}")
+        s.sendall(chunk)
+        sent += len(chunk)
+s.settimeout(300)   # the last page-cache flush happens before the reply
+reply = b""
+while b"\n" not in reply:
+    d = s.recv(4096)
+    if not d:
+        break
+    reply += d
+line = reply.split(b"\n")[0].decode(errors="replace").strip()
+dt = time.time() - t0
+print(f"device: {line!r} ({sent / dt / 1e6:.1f} MB/s)")
+if line != f"ok {n}":
+    sys.exit(f"put failed: expected 'ok {n}'")
+PY
 
 if [ "$VERIFY" = 1 ]; then
+	# Drop the page cache so the read-back comes from UFS, not RAM.
+	tab "write /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches 3" | grep -q '^ok' ||
+		{ echo "ERROR: drop_caches failed, read-back would not prove the write" >&2; exit 1; }
 	echo "Verifying (reading $LEN bytes back and comparing sha256)..."
-	WANT=$(sha256sum "$RAW" | cut -d' ' -f1)
-	BACK=$(mktemp --suffix=.raw)
-	trap 'rm -f "${RAW##*/}" "$BACK" 2>/dev/null; rm -f "$BACK"' EXIT
-	# tab-get reads exactly LEN bytes from the device node.
-	"$TAB_GET" "$DEV" "$BACK" "$LEN"
-	GOT=$(sha256sum "$BACK" | cut -d' ' -f1)
+	GOT=$(flock "$LOCK" python3 -I - "$LL%$IFC" "$DEV" "$LEN" <<'PY'
+import hashlib, socket, sys
+addr, remote, n = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2], int(sys.argv[3])
+s = socket.create_connection((addr, 23), timeout=30)
+s.settimeout(60)
+buf = b""
+while not buf.endswith(b"> "):
+    d = s.recv(65536)
+    if not d:
+        sys.exit("console closed before the prompt")
+    buf += d
+s.sendall(f"cat {remote}\n".encode())
+h = hashlib.sha256()
+got = 0
+while got < n:
+    d = s.recv(min(1 << 20, n - got))
+    if not d:
+        sys.exit(f"console closed after {got} of {n} bytes")
+    h.update(d)
+    got += len(d)
+# Do not drain the rest of the partition: close now (the serving child gets
+# EPIPE/SIGPIPE and exits).
+s.close()
+print(h.hexdigest())
+PY
+)
 	if [ "$WANT" != "$GOT" ]; then
 		echo "VERIFY FAILED: wrote $WANT, read back $GOT" >&2
 		exit 1
@@ -82,11 +173,8 @@ fi
 cat <<EOF
 
 Done. The Duranium GPT is now written to $DEV.
-Next:
-  1. Reboot the tablet into U-Boot (the boot chain on BOOT), e.g.
-       $TAB "reboot normal"
-     U-Boot exposes sda31 as a whole disk via blkmap and runs "bootefi
-     bootmgr" -> systemd-boot -> the Duranium UKI.
-  2. First boot runs systemd-repart (creates the B-slot usr+verity and the
-     LUKS root, growing into the full 52 GiB) and then f0rmz for user setup.
+Next (see contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/README.md, "Test plan"):
+  flash the chainload BOOT image (uniLoader -> U-Boot, bring-up Linux as the
+  watchdog fallback) from the chainload track. U-Boot maps sda31 as a whole
+  disk with blkmap and runs systemd-boot from the nested ESP.
 EOF
